# E §10: explain of a fill take prints "the fill's v version if it has one, the arcs in order, the remaining supply
# and demand before and after each take" (layout: this interpreter's).  The L §5.12 example fill of L5_12_fill
# (hand-checked there from the Procedure: takes 30, 70, 0, 10, 40 for ewa, in the order (o, t), ties by pos(sx)); jan's
# credits are 0, so its takes are 0 ("A take is 0 wherever ... R_s or Q_d is known to be 0").  x1: (ewa 2021; ewa
# 2022) takes min(40, 80) = 40.00 PLN.  x2: (2023; 2020) fails t >= o - 1, so it isn't an arc: 0 (Outputs).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index payers = [ewa, jan]
index yrs = year 2020..2023
input credit[sx in payers, o in yrs]: money PLN
input room[dx in payers, t in yrs]: money PLN
input carry_years: int

fill absorb
  supply credit[sx, o] for sx in payers, o in yrs
  demand room[dx, t] for dx in payers, t in yrs
  arc sx == dx and t >= o - 1 and t - o <= carry_years
  order o, t ties by pos(sx)

version v
  cite s
  governs 2020..
  known 2020-01-01
  credit[ewa, 2020] = 100.00 PLN
  credit[ewa, 2021] = 50.00 PLN
  credit[ewa, 2022] = 0.00 PLN
  credit[ewa, 2023] = 0.00 PLN
  credit[jan, *] = 0.00 PLN
  room[ewa, 2020] = 30.00 PLN
  room[ewa, 2021] = 80.00 PLN
  room[ewa, 2022] = 80.00 PLN
  room[ewa, 2023] = 0.00 PLN
  room[jan, *] = 10.00 PLN
  carry_years = 1

ask x1: explain absorb.taken[ewa, 2021, ewa, 2022] law 2026-06-30
ask x2: explain absorb.taken[ewa, 2023, ewa, 2020] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
x1: 40.00 PLN
  fill absorb, no v
  arcs in order:
    1. (ewa, 2020; ewa, 2020): supply 100.00 PLN, demand 30.00 PLN; takes 30.00 PLN; then supply 70.00 PLN, demand 0.00 PLN
    2. (jan, 2020; jan, 2020): supply 0.00 PLN, demand 10.00 PLN; takes 0.00 PLN; then supply 0.00 PLN, demand 10.00 PLN
    3. (ewa, 2020; ewa, 2021): supply 70.00 PLN, demand 80.00 PLN; takes 70.00 PLN; then supply 0.00 PLN, demand 10.00 PLN
    4. (jan, 2020; jan, 2021): supply 0.00 PLN, demand 10.00 PLN; takes 0.00 PLN; then supply 0.00 PLN, demand 10.00 PLN
    5. (ewa, 2021; ewa, 2020): supply 50.00 PLN, demand 0.00 PLN; takes 0.00 PLN; then supply 50.00 PLN, demand 0.00 PLN
